# The tools for agencies (tests/t1/museum_editor_tools.sh), on the project of the table session (golden/museum-editor/table.json) in a folder
# with its photograph. What the menu bar, the context menus and the system do is in session.system, at the same frames.
# The storyboard: every sequence selected, aligned at the top (menu bar, frame 6), nudged down, spread across (menu bar, frame 10), copied,
# pasted (the three copies are selected), nudged right by five steps.
4 key a meta
8 key ArrowDown
12 key c meta
14 key v meta
16 key ArrowRight shift
# The context menu of the first sequence: "Open its table".
20 move 350 200
21 right-down
22 right-up
# Its table: both media selected, aligned left (menu bar, frame 28), nudged, duplicated; the two copies aligned at the top (menu bar,
# frame 35), then cut.
26 key a meta
30 key ArrowRight
31 key ArrowDown shift
33 key d meta
39 key x meta
41 key Escape
# The context menu of the sequence beside it opens its table, where the two media are pasted.
44 move 600 182
45 right-down
46 right-up
50 key v meta
# Nothing selected; the context menu of the table: "Select all"; then Arrange > Centre vertically (menu bar, frame 60).
52 key Escape
54 move 800 300
55 right-down
56 right-up
# A picture is dropped on the window from outside the project (the system, frame 64): it is copied into the project folder and the
# question of "Add a file" opens on it; its source and its licence are typed, and it enters the library.
70 move 700 499
71 down
72 up
73 text https://example.org/estampe
75 move 700 562
76 down
77 up
78 text CC0
80 move 895 616
81 down
82 up
# Save.
88 key s meta
